{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"071eca35e0d356a7f1e2ddb19e6970aefe8a8886b33851ef89a6f7ab452a7a20","digest":{"component_or_area":"reconciler base-query fetcher","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","_build_snapshot","_fetch_project","_enrich_project","test_fetch_multi_project.py","test_one_project_base_query_failure_does_not_abort_pass","fetcher-project-fetch-failed","seen_keys","snapshot","jql_active","jql_done_recent","_validate_project_key","BackendPaginationStallError","alert_store"],"problem_keywords":["multi-project reconciler","base-query loop","resilience","per-project error isolation","fan-out","partial snapshot merge"],"propositions":["A single project's base-query transport error (ACLI 400/401/403/404/429/5xx/timeout) currently aborts the entire multi-project reconciliation pass and prevents other projects' issues from landing in the snapshot.","The base-query loop lacks per-project error isolation that already exists in the enrichment loop, causing a syntactically-valid but nonexistent project key to propagate a failure across all mapped projects.","Per-project transport errors must be caught, emitted as fetcher-project-fetch-failed alerts, and skipped without partial-key leakage into the shared snapshot or seen_keys.","A project's local query result must be merged atomically — if either the active or done-recent query fails, no partial keys from that project reach the shared snapshot where the differ would misread them as deletions."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787536963309826001,"uuid":"ac02c505-be8b-42b6-a411-a0a2bfa8b9f6"}